msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3626
msgid ""
"A function's resource usage depends on each of its callees' resource usage. "
"The expressions used to denote resource usage reflect this by propagating "
"each callees' equivalent expressions. Said expressions are emitted as "
"symbols by the compiler when compiling to either assembly or object format "
"and should not be overwritten or redefined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3632
msgid "The following describes all emitted function resource usage symbols:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3634
msgid "Function Resource Usage:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3639
msgid "Symbol"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3642
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3643
msgid "\\<function_name>.num_vgpr"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3644 ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3648
#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3652 ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3656
msgid "Integer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3645
msgid ""
"Number of VGPRs used by \\<function_name>, worst case of itself and its "
"callees' VGPR use"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3646
msgid ".set foo.num_vgpr, max(32, bar.num_vgpr, baz.num_vgpr)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3647
msgid "\\<function_name>.num_agpr"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3649
msgid ""
"Number of AGPRs used by \\<function_name>, worst case of itself and its "
"callees' AGPR use"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3650
msgid ".set foo.num_agpr, max(35, bar.num_agpr)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3651
msgid "\\<function_name>.numbered_sgpr"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3653
msgid ""
"Number of SGPRs used by \\<function_name>, worst case of itself and its "
"callees' SGPR use (without any of the implicitly used SGPRs)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3654
msgid ".set foo.num_sgpr, 21"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3655
msgid "\\<function_name>.private_seg_size"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3657
msgid ""
"Total stack size required for \\<function_name>, expression is the locally "
"used stack size + the worst case callee"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3658
msgid ""
".set foo.private_seg_size, 16+max(bar.private_seg_size, baz.private_seg_size)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3659
msgid "\\<function_name>.uses_vcc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3660 ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3664
#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3668 ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3672
#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3676
msgid "Bool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3661
msgid "Whether \\<function_name>, or any of its callees, uses vcc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3662
msgid ".set foo.uses_vcc, or(0, bar.uses_vcc)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3663
msgid "\\<function_name>.uses_flat_scratch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3665
msgid ""
"Whether \\<function_name>, or any of its callees, uses flat scratch or not"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3666
msgid ".set foo.uses_flat_scratch, 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3667
msgid "\\<function_name>.has_dyn_sized_stack"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3669
msgid "Whether \\<function_name>, or any of its callees, is dynamically sized"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3670
msgid ".set foo.has_dyn_sized_stack, 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3671
msgid "\\<function_name>.has_recursion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3673
msgid "Whether \\<function_name>, or any of its callees, contains recursion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3674
msgid ".set foo.has_recursion, 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3675
msgid "\\<function_name>.has_indirect_call"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3677
msgid ""
"Whether \\<function_name>, or any of its callees, contains an indirect call"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3678
msgid ".set foo.has_indirect_call, max(0, bar.has_indirect_call)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3681
msgid ""
"Furthermore, three symbols are additionally emitted describing the "
"compilation unit's worst case (i.e, maxima) `num_vgpr`, `num_agpr`, and "
"`numbered_sgpr` which may be referenced and used by the aforementioned "
"symbolic expressions. These three symbols are `amdgcn.max_num_vgpr`, "
"`amdgcn.max_num_agpr`, and `amdgcn.max_num_sgpr`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3689
msgid "ABI Occupancy (Object Linking)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3691
msgid ""
"*ABI occupancy* is the resource-bounded occupancy of a separately compiled "
"function under the object-linking ABI: a floor on waves per EU, which is a "
"cap on the register budget. Callers and callees rely on this floor without "
"seeing each other's register usage. It is not the occupancy the function "
"achieves: a function may use fewer registers than the cap and therefore "
"achieve a higher occupancy. For example, the ABI occupancy may be 4 even "
"when the function achieves an occupancy of 10."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3699
msgid ""
"A caller with ABI occupancy `N` can call a callee only when the callee's ABI "
"occupancy is at least `N`. A lower ABI occupancy raises the callee's "
"register cap, which can exceed the register budget implied by the caller's "
"ABI occupancy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3704
msgid ""
"When object linking is enabled, the AMDGPU backend no longer assumes whole-"
"program visibility. The default ABI occupancy is the number of waves per EU "
"required to support a 1024-workitem workgroup:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3708
msgid ""
"`ceil(ceil(1024 / wavefront-size) / workgroup-SIMDs)`, where `workgroup-"
"SIMDs` is the number of SIMDs that a workgroup's waves run on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3711
msgid ""
"For example, on `gfx900` (wave64, 4 workgroup SIMDs) the default ABI "
"occupancy is `ceil(ceil(1024 / 64) / 4) = 4`, which caps VGPRs at "
"`getMaxNumVGPRs(4) = 64`. On a gfx12 target such as `gfx1200` (wave32, 4 "
"workgroup SIMDs), the default ABI occupancy is `ceil(ceil(1024 / 32) / 4) = "
"8`, which caps VGPRs at `getMaxNumVGPRs(8) = 192`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3717
msgid ""
"The `amdgpu_abi_waves_per_eu` module flag overrides the default ABI "
"occupancy floor for a module. A value lower than the default lowers that "
"floor and raises the register cap (a looser ABI contract). A value higher "
"than the default raises the floor and lowers the register cap (a stricter "
"ABI contract)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3722
msgid ""
"`amdgpu-flat-work-group-size` is ABI-significant. If a function carries this "
"attribute, the occupancy implied by its maximum flat workgroup size replaces "
"the default ABI occupancy for that function. It takes precedence over the "
"`amdgpu_abi_waves_per_eu` module flag, so it can either raise or lower the "
"occupancy floor and the matching register cap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3728
msgid ""
"`amdgpu-waves-per-eu` remains a hint. It cannot lower the ABI occupancy. A "
"hint that asks for fewer waves than the ABI occupancy is rejected and leaves "
"the floor and the register cap unchanged. A hint that asks for more waves "
"raises the ABI occupancy and lowers the register cap only when the backend "
"accepts it. A request above the hardware maximum, or outside the occupancy "
"range implied by the workgroup size and LDS, is rejected and leaves the "
"floor and the register cap unchanged. The raised value is still the floor, "
"not the occupancy the function achieves."
msgstr ""

