#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4874
msgid ""
"The AMDGPU backend generates `Elf64_Rela` relocation records for AMDHSA or "
"`Elf64_Rel` relocation records for Mesa/AMDPAL. Supported relocatable fields "
"are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4878 ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4947
#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4952 ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4962
#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4972 ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4977
#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4982 ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4987
#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4992 ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4997
msgid "`word32`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4880
msgid ""
"This specifies a 32-bit field occupying 4 bytes with arbitrary byte "
"alignment. These values use the same byte order as other word values in the "
"AMDGPU architecture."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4884 ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4957
#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4967 ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:5007
msgid "`word64`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4886
msgid ""
"This specifies a 64-bit field occupying 8 bytes with arbitrary byte "
"alignment. These values use the same byte order as other word values in the "
"AMDGPU architecture."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4890
msgid "Following notations are used for specifying relocation calculations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4892
msgid "**A**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4894
msgid ""
"Represents the addend used to compute the value of the relocatable field. If "
"the addend field is smaller than 64 bits then it is zero-extended to 64 bits "
"for use in the calculations below. (In practice this only affects `_HI` "
"relocation types on Mesa/AMDPAL, where the addend comes from the 32-bit "
"field but the result of the calculation depends on the high part of the full "
"64-bit address.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4901
msgid "**G**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4903
msgid ""
"Represents the offset into the global offset table at which the relocation "
"entry's symbol will reside during execution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4906
msgid "**GOT**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4908
msgid "Represents the address of the global offset table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4910
msgid "**P**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4912
msgid ""
"Represents the place (section offset for `et_rel` or address for `et_dyn`) "
"of the storage unit being relocated (computed using `r_offset`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4915
msgid "**S**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4917
msgid ""
"Represents the value of the symbol whose index resides in the relocation "
"entry. Relocations not using this must specify a symbol index of `STN_UNDEF`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4921
msgid "**B**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:4923
msgid ""
"Represents the base address of a loaded executable or shared object which is "
"the difference between the ELF address and the actual load address. "
"Relocations using this are only valid in executable or shared objects."
msgstr ""

